{"id": "EUVD-2026-102497", "enisaUuid": "c5a1a9be-2f3d-3d2d-9899-2e8158c43236", "description": "Peppermint through 0.5.5 contains a missing authorization vulnerability that allows any authenticated user to create time entries and attachments as other users by supplying a user id in the request body. Attackers can send POST requests to /api/v1/time/new or /api/v1/storage/ticket/:id/upload/single to attach files and time records to any ticket under another user's identity.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T21:43:43", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T01:47:26", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@hieuPenguinnn/peppermint-data-logs-missing-authorization", "https://github.com/Peppermint-Lab/peppermint/blob/0.5.5/apps/api/src/controllers/time.ts#L6-L27", "https://github.com/Peppermint-Lab/peppermint/blob/0.5.5/apps/api/src/controllers/storage.ts#L9-L35", "https://github.com/Peppermint-Lab/peppermint/blob/0.5.5/apps/api/src/main.ts#L57-L70", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/peppermint-through-0.5.5-missing-authorization-via-time-tracking-and-attachment-upload-endpoints"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111353", "GHSA-988q-6ph7-3qfp"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.25, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "45952020-ee48-3fd5-9c03-74663a913dc7", "product": {"name": "Peppermint", "vendor": {"name": "Peppermint Lab"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.5.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "3fd8be6a-ffd6-3de7-ba31-ae1f1b3a63fa", "vendor": {"name": "Peppermint-Lab"}}], "isExploited": false}